      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I was about to make my own report for this until I found this canny. Here are my reproduction steps.\n\n1. Use an avatar with Physbones that have IsAnimated disabled and uses colliders.\n\n2. Scale the avatar down to 0.2m.\n\n3. Physbones are now pointing outwards due to self collision. (Alternatively, just check the physbone debug.)\n\nAn avatar that is scaled and does not use IsAnimated on its Physbones will not have their Physbones updated to their new scale. This occurs immediately after scaling the avatar.\n\nHowever, if the avatar is reloaded or is late loaded by another player, the Physbones will look correct. This is probably because the Physbones loaded in at the current avatar scale.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
